1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,500
Connecting an autonomous agent to Supabase with

2
00:00:03,500 --> 00:00:06,720
MCP gives it superpowers over your database!

3
00:00:07,420 --> 00:00:09,740
Let's get started: head to your account settings

4
00:00:09,740 --> 00:00:11,740
and open Access Tokens.

5
00:00:14,600 --> 00:00:17,160
Click Generate new token and give it a

6
00:00:17,160 --> 00:00:19,720
name. Since we're just testing locally, let's

7
00:00:19,720 --> 00:00:21,700
keep it safe and set the expiration to

8
00:00:21,700 --> 00:00:24,760
24 hours—always best to keep demo credentials

9
00:00:24,760 --> 00:00:28,780
tightly scoped. Pick your organization, and select

10
00:00:28,780 --> 00:00:30,940
the Full access preset so our agent can

11
00:00:30,940 --> 00:00:34,220
inspect schemas, run migrations, and execute SQL

12
00:00:34,220 --> 00:00:35,720
without hitting permission walls.

13
00:00:39,640 --> 00:00:42,620
Hit Create token, copy the key to your

14
00:00:42,620 --> 00:00:45,260
clipboard, and confirm. Treat this like gold—Supabase

15
00:00:46,500 --> 00:00:48,240
will only show you this secret once!

16
00:00:53,720 --> 00:00:56,740
Awesome, with our token ready, let's hop right

17
00:00:56,740 --> 00:00:59,760
into Antigravity to plug Supabase into our agent's

18
00:00:59,760 --> 00:01:09,740
workspace! Now, paste your token right into the

19
00:01:09,740 --> 00:01:11,780
chat and tell your agent to configure the

20
00:01:11,560 --> 00:01:15,040
Supabase MCP server. Just hit send, and let

21
00:01:15,040 --> 00:01:17,520
Antigravity do the heavy lifting behind the scenes.

22
00:01:18,800 --> 00:01:20,920
And just like that, it's done!

23
00:01:21,580 --> 00:01:24,720
The agent configured the MCP server, authenticated

24
00:01:24,720 --> 00:01:27,000
via the CLI, and wired up our project

25
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:28,160
credentials in the local .env.

26
00:01:29,120 --> 00:01:31,340
Our database connection is officially live!

27
00:01:33,380 --> 00:01:35,240
Now let's put it to work.

28
00:01:35,900 --> 00:01:37,920
We ask the agent to create a project

29
00:01:37,920 --> 00:01:40,900
management schema with users, projects, and tasks,

30
00:01:41,400 --> 00:01:43,880
plus a few dummy rows so we can

31
00:01:43,880 --> 00:01:45,140
verify the data live.

32
00:01:46,460 --> 00:01:50,260
And boom! In seconds, the agent executes the

33
00:01:50,260 --> 00:01:53,600
migration via MCP, sets up all foreign keys,

34
00:01:54,080 --> 00:01:56,600
and seeds our test data directly into Postgres.

35
00:01:58,640 --> 00:02:00,780
Now, let's head over to Supabase to see

36
00:02:00,780 --> 00:02:04,100
the magic live. We open our project, jump

37
00:02:04,100 --> 00:02:06,520
into the Database tab, and open the Schema

38
00:02:06,520 --> 00:02:08,240
Visualizer. And look at that:

39
00:02:08,880 --> 00:02:11,440
all three tables, foreign keys, and relations

40
00:02:11,440 --> 00:02:13,920
were created completely autonomously in PostgreSQL!

41
00:02:18,700 --> 00:02:21,360
Back in Antigravity, we can see the seed

42
00:02:21,360 --> 00:02:23,560
data generated by the agent matches our schema

43
00:02:23,560 --> 00:02:26,900
perfectly. Giving your agent direct MCP superpowers

44
00:02:26,900 --> 00:02:28,660
to manage your database is that simple.

45
00:02:29,480 --> 00:02:31,880
Hit subscribe for more agent workflows, and see

46
00:02:31,880 --> 00:02:32,560
you in the next one!
